{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310686,"nonce":"7caLpfbfvLJgLD+lfrZ0uSc+3Gk=","title":"ggml-style interleaved repack GEMV REFUTED on M1 Pro 2026-06-12 — zero-LOC llama-bench ABBA showed no repack advantage (sign 3-3, median ...","message":"**Hypothesis (from the bandwidth-lever research workflow):** the remaining\nrayzor-vs-llama.cpp CPU decode gap was ggml's 4×8 interleaved repack GEMV\n(default since llama.cpp PR #17494, 2025-11), which reuses each loaded q8\nactivation span across interleaved weight rows. Research estimated +8-15%\n→ 88-94 tok/s, with a mandatory zero-LOC falsifier first.\n\n**Falsifier executed 2026-06-12 (llama-bench, brew ggml 0.13.1 build 9400,\nM1 Pro, Llama 3.2 1B Q4_K_M, tg128, -ngl 0 -t 8, repack vs `-ot '.*=CPU'`,\n113 tensors confirmed repacked via -v):**\n- Two sequential A/Bs contradicted each other (+7.3% then -7.7%), σ up to 21.\n- ABBA alternating pairs (6 pairs, r=3, 8s spacing):\n  deltas -3.0 / +4.0 / -27.0 / +12.7 / -0.1 / +0.8 → **sign 3-3, median\n  +0.4 — no effect above the ±3% llama-bench noise floor on this machine.**\n\n**Verdict:** repack port NOT justified on M1 Pro. The PR's +11-18% tg gain\npresumably materialises on other core configurations; on M1 Pro tg the\nper-row dotprod kernel is already at the same plateau (consistent with the\nsession's other finding that compute width saturates at 7 threads —\n[[perf-dispatch-threading-arc]]). 5th llama.cpp-mimicry candidate killed,\nfirst one killed for ~$0 by running the falsifier before the port.\n\n**Side-findings:**\n- Current llama.cpp tg128 on this machine: ~93-103 tok/s (both configs) —\n  the \"llama.cpp CPU = 86.9\" memory entry is stale (newer build). NOT\n  directly comparable to rayzor's 81.4 (600-token KV + server + streaming\n  overhead vs short-KV bare tg128). A matched-length comparison is needed\n  before quoting any rayzor-vs-llama.cpp gap number again.\n- `-ot '.*=CPU_REPACK'` is not a valid override target in this build; use\n  `-ot '.*=CPU'` to disable repack (verify with -v \"repack tensor\" count).\n- llama-bench single-invocation σ on this machine is 4-21 tok/s — ABBA\n  pairs with spacing are mandatory, single runs are meaningless.\n\n**State of the CPU lane after this:** bandwidth eliminated, act-quant\neliminated, repack refuted, compute width saturated, dispatch overhead\n~1-2μs/join. Remaining CPU items are crumbs (pre-quant setup NEON ~1-3%\nunmeasured; alloc churn ≤2.3%). The only double-digit lever standing is\nthe **Metal decode arc** (llama.cpp Metal ~140 tok/s existence proof; M0\ngate = 3-day batched-compute-encoder spike, 200 dispatches + 1 wait\n\u003c 1.5ms, before any shader work).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_repack_gemv_no_win` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}